    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210">

                <pb facs="0302" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg218"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beaupré to Mr.
                            Hay</hi>,</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation at Bogotá</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1903-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic">October
                                31, 1903</hi></date>. (Received November 6,
                    1903.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Congress adjourned to-day. No action has been taken upon the last report
                    concerning the canal. Therefore nothing more than the vote of August 12
                    rejecting treaty done.</p>
                <p>The people here in great anxiety over conflicting reports of secession movements
                    in the Cauca and Panama.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
